// The office how-to guide the Ask WorkFleet chat answers from.
// Written from the code on 2026-11-14 (every page under app/admin). When a
// page changes in a way an office worker would notice, update its section
// here too, or the chat will describe the old screen.

export const OFFICE_GUIDE = "# WorkFleet office guide\n\nThis guide covers the office side of WorkFleet: the pages under the office menu, used by admins and supervisors. It is written from the app's own code. Button and label names are shown in quotes exactly as they appear on screen.\n\n## Getting around\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\n- Admins see every menu item. Supervisors (\"Office Staff / Supervisor\") see the same menu except Invoices, Cleaners, Onboarding, Payroll, Accidents and incidents, and Insights, which are admins only.\n- Invoices is shown only to one named admin account, not to every admin.\n- Accounts set to \"Inventory only\" (or staff given the stock permission) see only the stock screens, not the rest of the office.\n- The menu is grouped: Dashboard, Notifications, Messages, Announcements and AI assistant at the top; then Work (Rota, Shift cover, Team tasks, Projects, Requests); Clients (Clients, Quotes, Invoices); People (Cleaners, Onboarding, Payroll, Training); Records (Templates, Documents, Inventory, Key register, Accidents and incidents, Insights, Reports, Data reports); and Help.\n- \"Search\" at the top of the menu (or Ctrl K) finds a client, site, cleaner or page. Supervisors can search clients and sites but not staff pages.\n- The bell icon in the menu header turns on push notifications for this device. The people icon (\"Who's online\") shows who else is online.\n- The page size control at the bottom of the menu makes the page smaller, bigger or back to normal size.\n- \"Log out\" is at the bottom of the menu.\n- If a deactivated account is still signed in, it is signed out the next time a page loads.\n\n---\n\n## Dashboard (Dashboard) - page: /admin\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office. The \"Staff hours\" panel is shown to admins only.\n\nThe dashboard greets you by name and refreshes itself every two minutes. The \"Updated ...\" button fetches the latest figures straight away.\n\nWhat is on it:\n- Four figures across the top: \"Jobs today\", \"Working now\", \"Hours booked\" and \"Requests open\". Each one is a link (to the Rota, Cleaners or Requests).\n- \"Today\": today's jobs, grouped into \"On site now\", \"Hours to check\", \"Missed\" and \"Coming up\". A job with nobody on it is marked so you can open it and put someone on it. A job that started without a clock-in shows \"Not clocked in - ... late\".\n- \"Tomorrow\": how many jobs, how many \"need a cleaner\", how many staff are \"away\", and when the first job starts and the last finishes.\n- \"Later this week\": jobs in the next week.\n- \"Needs attention\": the most urgent things first. These include kit top-up and issue requests, client and 1:1 review reminders, certifications expiring or expired, contract renewals due, and \"No access codes for N sites\".\n- \"Who's on now\": who is clocked in, plus \"on holiday\" and \"not working today\" counts you can click to see names.\n- \"Staff hours\" (admins only): live hours for a chosen period, split into \"Completed\", \"Scheduled\" and \"Remaining\", with the top few people. It also flags shifts where nobody clocked in, or claims to confirm.\n\nHow to clear a kit top-up or issue from the dashboard\n1. Find it under \"Needs attention\".\n2. Click \"Mark sent\" (kit top-up) or \"Resolved\" (issue). Or open it and click \"Mark resolved\".\n3. It comes off the list. For a note to the cleaner, use Requests instead (see Requests).\n\nHow to clear a review reminder\n1. Under \"Needs attention\", click \"Done\" on the reminder.\n\nHow to fix \"No access codes for N sites\"\n1. Click the line to open the list of sites.\n2. Click a site. It opens the client's page.\n3. Press \"Access\" on that site and add the details (see Clients).\n\nOther buttons:\n- \"Find a client, site or cleaner\" opens search.\n- \"Today's report\" opens Reports.\n- \"New job\" opens the Rota with the new job form.\n- \"Close payroll\" (in Staff hours) opens Payroll. The dashboard figures keep changing; Payroll is where a period is locked.\n\n---\n\n## Notifications (Notifications) - page: /admin/notifications\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nEverything the app has told you, newest first: requests, messages, dropped shifts, claims and so on. Notifications are removed automatically after 30 days.\n\nHow to clear notifications\n1. Click the dismiss button on one notification. It stays in your history for 30 days.\n2. Or click \"Dismiss all (N)\" to mark every notification as read.\n\n---\n\n## Messages (Messages) - page: /admin/messages\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nThere are two views: \"Clients\" and \"Staff\".\n\nHow to reply to a client\n1. Click \"Clients\".\n2. Open the conversation. Clients write in from their client portal.\n3. Type in \"Type a reply...\" and click \"Send\".\n\nHow to start a chat with a member of staff\n1. Click \"Staff\".\n2. Click \"+ New chat\".\n3. Under \"Start a chat with...\", pick the person. The list shows admins and cleaners.\n4. Type in \"Type a message...\" and click \"Send\".\n\n---\n\n## Announcements (Announcements) - page: /admin/announcements\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nAn announcement is a message to every cleaner. It pops up the next time they open the app, until they tap \"Got it\".\n\nHow to send an announcement\n1. Under \"New message\", fill in \"Headline\" (required, up to 120 characters) and \"Message\".\n2. Tick \"Also send a phone notification\" if you want it to go to the phones of anyone with alerts on.\n3. Click \"Send to all staff (N)\". N is the number of active staff it goes to.\n4. Confirm. The app says it will pop up when they next open the app.\n5. You see \"Message sent to all staff.\"\n\nAfter sending\n- Under \"Sent\", each message shows \"Seen by X of Y\". Click it to see who has \"Seen\" it and who has \"Not seen yet\".\n- \"Stop showing\" hides the message. Anyone who has not opened the app yet will not see it.\n- \"Show again\" puts a stopped message back.\n\n---\n\n## AI assistant (AI assistant) - page: /admin/assistant\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office. Only admins can change Company facts.\n\nThe assistant writes a draft document from a plain request. It asks anything it needs to know first, then writes a draft you can finish and download.\n\nHow to draft a document\n1. Type what you need in \"What do you need?\". You can click one of the example requests to start from it.\n2. Optional: click \"More options - client, project, files, pasted text\". There you can choose:\n   - \"Kind of document\" (or \"Let the AI decide\"). Kinds include letters and emails to clients, a reply to a complaint, method statements, risk assessment outlines, job adverts, notices to staff, policies, procedures, tender answers, mobilisation plans, social value statements, case studies and \"Something else\".\n   - \"Client\" and \"Site\". For a client, the AI sees their name, contact, site addresses, recent visit counts and ratings. It never sees door codes or access notes.\n   - \"Project\".\n   - \"Files to read\" (from the project's files or the Documents library). Only PDF, text and image files can be read. Save Word files as PDF first.\n   - \"Paste text (optional)\", for an email, tender question or notes.\n3. Click \"Next\".\n4. Answer the questions it asks. Leave any you can't answer; it will leave a blank. Click \"Write it\", or \"Skip, just write it\". \"Start again\" goes back.\n5. The draft appears. Writing can take up to a minute.\n\nFinishing the draft\n- Blanks the AI could not fill are listed underneath. Type the answer and click \"Fill in\".\n- \"Edit the text\" lets you change the draft by hand. Click \"Done editing\" when finished.\n- \"Want it different?\" - type a change (for example \"shorter\") and click \"Rewrite\". Rewriting starts from the text as it is now, including your edits.\n- \"Download Word\" saves a Word file. \"Copy text\" copies it.\n- If you chose a project, \"Save to project notes\" saves it to that project.\n- \"New request\" starts a new one.\n- If it says the draft was cut off, ask for something shorter.\n- \"Recent drafts\" lists saved drafts. Click one to open it, or use the bin icon to delete it.\n\nYou can also open the assistant from a client's page (\"Draft a document with AI\" in the menu) or from a project (\"Open the AI assistant\").\n\n### Company facts - page: /admin/assistant/facts\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office can read it; admins only can change it.\n\nThe assistant treats everything here as true and uses it in every draft. The sections are \"About us\", \"Cover and certificates\", \"How we work\" and \"Letters and style\". Fields include services, areas covered, insurance, certifications you hold, staff vetting, training, quality checks, complaints, cover for sickness and holidays, health and safety, who signs letters and house style.\n\n- \"Things the AI must NEVER claim\" is special: the AI is told never to state or hint at anything written there, even if asked.\n- Click \"Save N changes\" (or \"Save\" at the bottom). You see \"Saved. Every new draft will use these.\"\n- The assistant page shows a \"Fill them in\" prompt until the facts are filled in. \"Company facts\" on the assistant page opens this page.\n\n---\n\n## Rota (Work → Rota) - page: /admin/rota\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nThe rota shows every job and training session.\n\nViews and controls\n- Arrows move back or forward a week (or a day in Day view). \"Today\" jumps back.\n- \"By cleaner\": a row per cleaner, days across. \"By time\": the week on the clock.\n- \"Week\" or \"Day\". Day view shows each cleaner's free time between jobs as dashed slots (free time counts between 07:00 and 18:00).\n- Staff order: \"A-Z\", \"Most hours\" or \"Arrange\". In Arrange, drag the grip by a name to move someone up or down. The Arrange order is shared with everyone in the office.\n- The key: Booked, Done, On site, Needs attention, Away, Free to book. Each client has its own colour down the edge of its jobs.\n- \"tight travel gaps\" counts gaps between one cleaner's jobs that are shorter than the drive. Click it to see them under \"Not enough time to get there\". This is an estimate from the property pins.\n- \"How the rota works\" folds out short instructions.\n- \"Change log\" and \"Job history\" links are at the foot of the rota.\n\n### How to book a new job\n\n1. Click \"New job\" (or, in By cleaner view, point at a day and press \"+\" to book that person; in Day view, press a free slot).\n2. Under \"What is this?\", choose \"Job for a client\" (or \"Training\", see below).\n3. Choose the \"Client\". Then the \"Address\": pick one from \"Saved for this client\" or type a new one. A new address is saved for next time.\n4. Set \"Date\", \"Time\" and \"Duration\" (pick a preset or \"Custom\").\n5. Optional: \"Checklist template (optional)\" to copy a template's tasks onto the job.\n6. Under \"Cleaners\", click each person to put on the job.\n7. With two or more cleaners, \"Hours each\" shows an even split. Tick \"Set each person's hours\" to set them by hand. The app warns if they don't add up to the job length.\n8. To repeat it, tick \"Repeat this job\" (see below).\n9. Click \"Add job\". Anyone you assigned is notified.\n\nChecks when booking or assigning\n- If a cleaner is already booked around that time, you see \"Scheduling conflict\". Choose \"Save anyway\" / \"Assign anyway\" / \"Create anyway\" or cancel.\n- If they have approved holiday or unavailability that day, you see \"Time off conflict\" with \"Schedule anyway\".\n- If the drive from their previous job is too tight, you see \"Not enough time to get there\" with \"Assign anyway\".\n\n### How to set up a repeating job\n\n1. In the new job form, tick \"Repeat this job\".\n2. Choose \"Frequency\": \"Daily\", \"Weekly\" or \"Monthly\", and \"Every N days/weeks/months\".\n3. For weekly, tick the days under \"On these days\" (at least one).\n4. Under \"Ends\", choose \"After a number of times\" or \"On a date\".\n5. The form shows how many jobs it will book and the first and last date.\n6. A series is capped at 104 occurrences. Each visit can be moved, reassigned or deleted on its own afterwards.\n\n### How to book training\n\n1. Click \"New job\" and choose \"Training\".\n2. Fill in \"What the training is\", \"Where\", \"Who's running it\".\n3. Optional: \"Certificate earned (optional)\" and \"Expires\". Everyone who checks in to the session gets that certificate added to their record when it finishes. Leave it blank for a toolbox talk.\n4. Pick who is attending and click \"Add job\".\n\n### How to open and change a job\n\nClick a job on the rota. The job panel shows:\n- \"Address\". Changing it updates the address for every job at this property, not just this one.\n- \"Date\", \"Time\", \"Duration\". These can only be changed while the job is still scheduled. Once it has started or finished, the panel says its date and time can't be changed; add a new job instead.\n- \"Notes\". Cleaners see these notes on their job screen.\n- \"Room refreshes\" and \"+ Add a room refresh\". Each refresh has a room name and a length. It shows as its own line on the invoice breakdown. Refreshes that add up to more than the visit is booked for are refused; make the visit longer.\n- Click \"Save changes\".\n\nMoving a job by dragging\n- Drag a job to a new day or time. On a touchscreen, press and hold first.\n- In By cleaner view, drag a job to another day, or onto another person's row to hand it to them. The time stays the same.\n- Only scheduled jobs can be dragged. The usual clash and time-off checks still run, and the cleaner is told it was moved.\n\n### How to add or remove a cleaner on a job\n\n1. Open the job.\n2. Under \"Assigned staff\", choose from \"Add a cleaner...\" and click \"Add\". They get a notification about the new shift.\n3. To take someone off, click \"Remove\" next to their name. They are told it has been unassigned.\n\nOn a recurring job, Remove and Add ask which visits you mean:\n- Remove offers \"Just this visit\", \"This visit and N later in this series\", and \"This visit and all N later at this site\". Earlier and finished visits are never changed, and nobody else is taken off.\n- Add offers \"Just this visit\" or \"This visit and all N later ones\" (the later ones they are not yet on). If any of those visits clash, overlap time off or have tight travel, you are asked \"Check before adding\" first.\n\nSetting one person's hours on a job\n1. Click \"Hours\" next to their name.\n2. Enter the hours and click \"Save\". Their rota, hours page and payroll use this instead of an even split.\n3. \"Even split\" goes back to sharing the job length evenly.\n\nFinished jobs\n- When a visit is completed or missed, the staff on it can't be changed. To correct what someone is paid for it, use \"Hours\".\n\n### To-do list, check-ins and photos on a job\n\n- \"To-do list\": add a task and click \"Add\", remove one with \"Remove\", or pick \"Apply a template...\" and click \"Apply\" to copy every task from a template.\n- \"Check-ins\" shows who checked in and out and when. \"location unverified\" means the property has a pin but the check-in had no location.\n- \"Photos\" shows the photos taken. If an area check ran, \"Photo check at check-out\" shows which areas were photographed and whether they checked out anyway.\n\n### How to change a recurring series\n\n1. Open a visit in the series.\n2. Under \"Recurring series\", click \"Edit this + future\".\n3. Change \"Frequency\", days, \"Time\", \"Until\" or \"Duration\".\n4. Click \"Save series\" and confirm \"Apply\" in \"Change this series\". The message lists any visits that will be deleted for good.\n5. Changes apply from this visit onward. Earlier visits, visits that have already happened, and visits moved to a different day by hand are not touched.\n6. To change who does it, use Remove or Add under \"Assigned staff\".\n\n### How to delete a job\n\n1. Open the job. The delete area is at the bottom of the panel.\n2. Click \"Delete job\" for just this one, or \"Delete this + future\" on a recurring job.\n3. You are asked twice. The second message says the visit, its tasks and any check-ins will be deleted for good. Click \"Yes, delete it\" (or \"Yes, delete N\").\n\nRules:\n- A completed or missed visit can't be deleted. The panel says it stays on the record.\n- On a finished visit in a series, \"Delete future visits\" deletes the visits after it. Completed and missed ones are always kept.\n- Visits before the one you opened are kept.\n\n### Job history - page: /admin/rota/history\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nA table of jobs with Date, Client, Address, Staff, Duration and Status. Search by address, client or staff, and filter by status (\"All statuses\", Scheduled, In Progress, Completed, Missed).\n\n### Change log - page: /admin/audit\n\nWho can use it: admins only in practice. The page is opened from the rota's \"Change log\" link (it is not in the menu), and the log can only be read by admins, so a supervisor sees it empty.\n\nEvery job, cleaner assignment, recurring series, property and client added, moved or deleted, most recent 1000 first. Search by address, client, cleaner or who made the change, and filter by type of change. Each line says who did it and how (for example \"In the app\", or \"Server / script\"). Changes are recorded from the time the log was switched on.\n\n---\n\n## Shift cover (Work → Shift cover) - page: /admin/cover\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nShifts that need someone. Free cleaners can ask for them, and you approve who gets each one.\n\nHow a cover request starts\n- A cleaner opens their shift and taps \"Can't make this shift\". The shift stays theirs until someone else is approved for it, and the office is told straight away.\n- Approving time off can also put the person's upcoming shifts out for cover (see Requests).\n- You can open one yourself (below).\n\nHow to open a cover request yourself\n1. Click \"Request cover\".\n2. Under \"Shift\", choose an upcoming shift. Only upcoming scheduled client jobs are listed, not training.\n3. Optional: \"Reason (optional)\".\n4. Click \"Open cover request\". Staff are notified.\n\nHow to approve someone who asked\n1. Under \"Needs cover (N)\", find the shift. \"Asked for this shift\" lists who has asked.\n2. Click \"Approve\" next to a name. The shift goes on their rota, it comes off the original cleaner, and everyone else who asked is told.\n3. Or click \"Turn down\" for a person. The shift stays open for others and they are told it went to someone else.\n\nHow to assign it directly\n1. Click \"Assign\" on the shift.\n2. \"Best matches\" lists who fits, with reasons, and marks the \"Best fit\". \"Said no\" marks people who turned it down. Click \"Assign\" next to one.\n3. Or pick anyone under \"Or choose anyone\" and click \"Assign and close request\".\n4. The cleaner is notified. If someone was releasing the shift, they come off it.\n\nHow to cancel a request\n1. Click \"Cancel\" on the shift and confirm. The shift stays with whoever is on it now.\n\nNotes:\n- Only active cleaners who are set to be offered cover appear in the list of people to assign (see Cleaners, \"Offer them shifts that need covering\").\n- \"Recently closed\" shows requests that were covered or closed.\n\nWhat cleaners see: open shifts appear under \"Shifts needing cover\" on their home screen. They tap \"Ask for this shift\" (or \"Not me\" to hide it). They are told the office confirms who gets it. Their own requests appear under \"Your cover requests\", where they can withdraw them.\n\n---\n\n## Team tasks (Work → Team tasks) - page: /admin/tasks\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nInternal work assigned between admins and supervisors. Your own list (\"My Tasks\") is first, everyone else's below. Cleaners do not see these.\n\nHow to add a task\n1. Click \"+ New task\".\n2. Fill in \"Title\", and optionally \"Description (optional)\".\n3. Choose \"Assign to\" and optionally \"Due date (optional)\".\n4. Click \"Add task\".\n\nManaging tasks\n- Filter with \"Open\", \"Done\" or \"All\".\n- Change a task's status with its dropdown: \"To Do\", \"In Progress\" or \"Done\".\n- \"Delete\" removes a task after you confirm.\n\n---\n\n## Projects (Work → Projects) - page: /admin/projects\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nProjects hold tenders, new contract start-ups, deep cleans, certifications, internal work and anything else with a goal and a deadline. Each has tasks, key dates, notes and files.\n\nHow to start a project\n1. Click \"+ New project\".\n2. Fill in \"Name\" and choose \"Type\": \"Tender or bid\", \"New contract start-up\", \"Deep clean\", \"Certification (e.g. ISO)\", \"Internal\" or \"Other\".\n3. Set the date field. Its name depends on the type (for example \"Submission deadline\", \"Contract start date\", \"Deep clean date\", \"Certification audit date\" or \"Target date\").\n4. Optional: \"Client (optional)\", \"Site (optional)\", \"Owner\", and \"What is it for? (optional)\".\n5. For types with suggested tasks, tick \"Start with N suggested tasks\" to add them. Due dates are counted back from the date you set. You can rename, delete or add tasks afterwards.\n6. Click \"Create project\".\n\nFinding projects\n- Filter with \"Open\", \"Finished\" or \"All\", and by type.\n- A client's page also lists its projects.\n\n### Project page - /admin/projects/[id]\n\n- \"Edit\" changes the name, type, date, client, site, owner and description. Click \"Save\".\n- \"Status\": Planning, In progress, On hold, Done or Cancelled. For tenders, \"Outcome\": Not decided, Won, Lost or Withdrawn. Changes are noted in the history.\n- \"Tasks\": type in \"Add a task...\", choose who (\"Anyone\" or a person) and a due date, click \"Add\". Tick a task to mark it done. Click a task to edit it (\"Task\", \"Assigned to\", \"Due\", \"Notes\", then \"Save\", or \"Delete\"). \"Show done (N)\" / \"Hide done (N)\" toggles finished tasks.\n- \"Notes and history\": add a note and click \"Add note\". The app also logs events here (status changes, tasks done, files added, AI use).\n- \"Key dates\": name and date, then \"Add date\". Tick to mark done; bin icon to remove.\n- \"Files\": \"Upload\" one or more files. Click a file to open or download it; bin icon to delete it.\n- To delete the whole project, use the \"...\" menu and \"Delete project\". This deletes all its tasks, dates, notes and files and can't be undone.\n\nAI tools on a project\n- AI tools are off until you click \"Switch AI tools on\". For a tender you are asked to check the tender documents first, because some ban AI or require you to declare it. Every use is noted in the history. \"Switch off\" turns it off again.\n- \"Suggest tasks from a file\": upload the document to Files first (PDF, text or image; Word and Excel files are not listed). Choose the file and click \"Suggest tasks\". Tick the ones you want and click \"Add N to the project\". Nothing is added until you choose it.\n- \"Ask a question\": type a question, optionally tick files to read, click \"Ask\".\n- \"Summarise where it stands\": a summary of what is done, next, late or at risk.\n- \"Draft something\": choose \"What kind of writing?\" and click \"Write a draft\". Then \"Copy\", \"Word\", \"Save as a note\", or type a change and \"Rewrite\".\n- \"Open the AI assistant\" links to the full assistant with this project chosen.\n- Answers and drafts are marked as AI output. Check every fact before using it.\n\n---\n\n## Requests (Work → Requests) - page: /admin/requests\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nEverything waiting on a decision from the office. The page has four groups, each with tabs and counts:\n- Staff: \"Kit and issues\", \"Time off\".\n- Hours: \"Time extensions\", \"Hours to check\", \"Missed clock-ins\", \"Amend hours\", \"Absence record\".\n- Clients: \"Reschedules\", \"Client requests\", \"Pause requests\".\n- Safety and sites: \"Emergency log\", \"Property pins\".\n\n### Kit and issues\n\nCleaners send kit top-up requests and report issues from the app.\n1. Filter with \"Open\", \"Resolved\" or \"All\".\n2. Click \"Mark resolved\", add an optional \"Resolution note (optional)\", and click \"Confirm resolved\". The cleaner is told what you did.\n3. \"Reopen\" puts a resolved one back.\n\n### Time off\n\nHow to approve or decline a request\n1. Filter with \"Pending\", \"Approved\", \"Declined\" or \"All\".\n2. Click \"Approve\" or \"Decline\".\n3. Add an optional note and click \"Confirm Approval\" or \"Confirm Decline\".\n4. If the person is booked on shifts during that time, you see \"Shifts during this time off\". Approving with shifts still to come offers \"Approve and find cover\": those shifts go on Shift cover and are offered to the other cleaners. Otherwise it offers \"Approve anyway\".\n5. The cleaner is told the decision.\n\nSome requests show \"Approved by the app (automatically)\".\n\nHow to mark someone off yourself (for when they rang in)\n1. Click \"+ Mark time off\".\n2. Choose \"Who\" and \"Type\" (\"Holiday\" or \"Unavailable\"). Subcontractors can only be marked unavailable, because no holiday accrues for them.\n3. Set \"From\" and \"To\".\n4. For holiday, check \"Holiday hours\". If they are booked on those days, it fills in the booked hours; otherwise enter what they normally work.\n5. Optional: \"Reason (optional)\" and \"Note to them (optional)\".\n6. If they are booked on shifts in that time, you see \"Shifts during this time off\" with \"Save and find cover\" (or \"Save anyway\" if none are still to come).\n7. Click \"Mark as on holiday\" or \"Mark as unavailable\". It goes in already approved and they are told.\n\n### Time extensions\n\nCleaners on site can ask for more time.\n1. Click \"Approve\", \"Decline\" or \"Suggest alternative\".\n2. For an alternative, set a new date, time and duration.\n3. Add an optional note and click \"Confirm Approval\" / \"Confirm Decline\" / \"Confirm Suggestion\".\n\n### Hours to check\n\nShifts where someone clocked well under the booked time. These are held: they pay nothing until you decide. Clear them before a pay run.\n- \"Hours are right\": they worked the full shift and clocked out early. The booked hours are paid.\n- \"Correct it\": enter how long it actually ran (minutes). This rewrites the job's booked duration, which pay and holiday are both worked out from.\n\n### Missed clock-ins\n\nA shift nobody clocked into pays nothing and earns no holiday. Anything still pending on pay day is paid as zero. Payroll will not close while anyone here is undecided.\n\nThere are three lists:\n- \"Only some of the team clocked in\": on a shared shift, a colleague clocked in and these people did not. They are unpaid and the shift counts as missed for them. For each person choose \"What happened?\" and click \"Record\" (unpaid), or click \"They worked it\" to pay them their share.\n- \"Nobody clocked in\": no one has asked about these. Choose a reason and click \"Record\", or click \"They worked it\", add \"How do you know? (optional, shown to the cleaner)\", and click \"Record as worked\". This pays the shift and accrues holiday.\n- \"Claims from staff\": cleaners who tapped \"I worked this — I forgot to clock in\". Click \"Approve\" or \"Decline\", add an optional note, then \"Confirm approval\" or \"Confirm decline\". Approving records the shift as worked and puts the hours back.\n\nThe reasons are \"Client cancelled\" (applies to everyone on the job), \"Off sick\", \"Authorised absence\", \"Turned away on site\" and \"Did not turn up\". All of them leave the shift unpaid. Use \"They worked it\" if you decide to pay it. \"Undo\" removes a recorded reason so the shift needs a decision again.\n\n### Amend hours\n\nEvery completed job since the last payroll close, one line per person at their share of the booked time.\n1. Click \"Amend\" on a line.\n2. Enter the minutes to pay and a reason. The reason is required and is shown to them.\n3. Click \"Save\". \"Booked share\" removes the amendment.\n- It changes that person only. Anything already sent to payroll comes through as an adjustment on the next run.\n\n### Absence record\n\nEvery missed shift that has been accounted for, one entry per person, with the reason and who recorded it. Filter by \"Last 90 days\" or \"All time\", and by person. \"Undo\" removes an entry and sends the shift back to Missed clock-ins.\n\n### Reschedules (from clients)\n\n1. Click \"Approve\" or \"Decline\", add an optional note.\n2. Click \"Confirm approval\" to move the job to the date and time the client asked for, or \"Confirm decline\". If the cleaner already has a job at that time, you are warned first (\"Approve anyway\").\n\n### Client requests\n\n1. Click \"Mark resolved\", add an optional note, and click \"Confirm resolved\". The client sees the note.\n2. \"Reopen\" puts it back.\n\n### Pause requests\n\nClients can ask to pause their cleans.\n1. Click \"Approve\" or \"Decline\", add an optional note, and confirm.\n2. Approving does not cancel jobs already booked in that period. Check the rota yourself.\n\n### Emergency log\n\nAlerts raised by cleaners. Click \"Respond\". The cleaner is told help is on the way. \"View location\" shows where they were. Filter with \"Open\", \"Acknowledged\" or \"All\".\n\n### Property pins\n\nA cleaner checked in from outside the geofence and says the pin is wrong, or checked in at a property with no pin.\n1. Click \"View on map\" to check.\n2. Click \"Move pin here\" and confirm \"Move pin\". Check-in for every future visit is then measured from there.\n3. Or click \"Keep pin\".\n\n---\n\n## Clients (Clients → Clients) - page: /admin/clients\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nHow to add a client\n1. Click \"+ New client\".\n2. Fill in \"Client / Business name\" (required), and optionally \"Contact name\", \"Phone\", \"Email\", \"Billing address\", \"Industry\" and \"Notes\".\n3. Click \"Add client\". The client's page opens. Add their sites there with \"+ Property\".\n\nFinding a client: search by name, contact, email or phone, and filter by industry.\n\n### Client page - /admin/clients/[id]\n\nAt the top:\n- \"Edit\" changes the client's details, including \"Contract value (£/year)\", \"Renewal date\" and \"Notice period before renewal (days)\". Click \"Save\".\n- The \"...\" menu has \"Draft a document with AI\", \"Export data\" (downloads everything held about the client, for a data request), \"Mark relationship ended\" / \"Clear end date\", and \"Delete client\".\n- The client's projects are listed with a link to \"All projects\".\n\nTabs: \"Properties\", \"Call log\", \"Monthly hours\", \"Reviews\", \"Clock-ins\" and \"Documents\".\n\nHow to add a property (site)\n1. On \"Properties\", click \"+ Property\".\n2. Fill in \"Address\", and optionally \"Notes (optional)\" and \"Access details (optional)\".\n3. Click \"Add property\".\n\nHow to record access details (alarm codes, key safes, how to get in)\n1. Click \"Access\" on the property.\n2. Type the details and click \"Save access details\".\n3. They are shown to the cleaner on their job screen for that property once they are assigned, and to the office here. Anything the client adds in their own portal appears separately.\n- A property with no access details shows a note saying cleaners see no codes for it.\n\nHow to set or move a map pin\n1. Click \"Set pin\" (no pin yet) or \"Location\".\n2. Search the address, then drag the pin (or tap the map) onto the front door.\n3. Optional: \"Check-in radius (metres)\". The default is 75. It must be between 25 and 2000. Widen it for a school, a farm, or anywhere the door is far from where phones get a fix.\n4. Click \"Save location\". Check-in is measured from the new pin.\n- Without a pin, check-in is not location-checked at that property.\n\nProperty checklist\n1. Click \"Checklist\" on the property.\n2. Enter a room and a task and click \"Add\". \"Delete\" removes one.\n- It is a room-by-room reference so any cleaner covering the property knows what \"done\" looks like.\n\nDeleting a property\n- Click \"Remove\" on the property. You are asked twice. If it has jobs, they are deleted too and this can't be undone.\n\nCall log\n1. On \"Call log\", choose \"Direction\" (\"Called them\" or \"They called us\").\n2. Fill in \"What was discussed\" and click \"Log call\". \"Remove\" deletes an entry.\n\nMonthly hours: hours and job counts per month from completed jobs.\n\nReviews (reminders)\n1. On \"Reviews\", click \"+ Reminder\".\n2. Set \"Due date\", tick \"Repeats yearly\" if needed, add notes, and click \"Add reminder\".\n3. \"Done\" marks it done. Yearly ones show \"Done (reset to next year)\" and roll forward. \"Delete\" removes it.\n- Due reminders appear on the Dashboard under \"Needs attention\".\n\nClock-ins: every check-in at the client's sites.\n\nDocuments shared with the client\n1. On \"Documents\", choose a \"Category\" (Health & Safety, Contract, Policy, Other).\n2. Choose files (PDF or Word). They upload straight away.\n3. Files here are visible only to that client in their client portal, not to other clients or to staff.\n4. Download or delete with the icons. Deleting means the client can no longer see it.\n\nEnding a relationship and deleting\n- \"Mark relationship ended\" records today as the end date. The client's contact details are automatically redacted 6 years later under the data retention policy. \"Clear end date\" undoes this.\n- \"Delete client\" deletes the client, all their properties and all their jobs for good. You are asked twice (\"Yes, delete everything\").\n\n---\n\n## Quotes (Clients → Quotes) - page: /admin/quotes\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office. The \"Settings\" menu (quote wording, company details, pricing settings) is admins only.\n\nHow to write a quote\n1. Click \"+ New quote\".\n2. \"Who's this for?\": \"An existing client\" (choose the client) or \"A new prospect\" (name, optional email and phone).\n3. Optional: \"Site address (optional)\". For a client you can pick a saved address.\n4. \"How is this priced?\":\n   - \"I'll enter the price myself\".\n   - \"Work it out from the property (one-off job)\": fill in service type, property type, condition, clean type, furnished, travel miles, room counts and extras. Click \"Use this price\" and \"Use this description\" to copy the results into the quote.\n   - \"Set out a shift pattern (staffed contract)\": add each shift with \"+ Add shift pattern\" (shift name, how often, days, start and end, operatives per shift, charge rate, optional note for the client) and the initial contract period. Click \"Use weekly charge as price\" and \"Use this description\".\n5. Fill in \"Description of work\", \"Price (£)\", \"This price is\" (the period), \"Valid until (optional)\" and \"Notes (optional)\". Notes are internal and not shown to the client.\n6. Click \"Add quote\" (or \"Save changes\" when editing).\n\nWorking with quotes\n- Filter with \"Open\", \"Decided\", \"All\" or \"Archived\".\n- Change the status with the dropdown on the quote: Draft, Sent, Accepted, Declined or Expired.\n- \"Why this price?\" shows the calculator breakdown, including profit and margin. \"Hide breakdown\" closes it.\n- \"Edit\" changes the quote.\n- \"PDF\" downloads a PDF to send. \"Word\" downloads a Word document you can edit first. The app does not send quotes itself.\n- \"Archive\" files a quote away. On an archived quote, \"Restore\" brings it back and \"Delete\" deletes it permanently. A quote must be archived before it can be deleted.\n\nSettings (admins only), from the \"Settings\" menu:\n- \"Quote wording\" opens the wording page (below).\n- \"Company details\": the company name, address and contact details printed on quotes. Changes affect documents generated from now on. Click \"Save details\".\n- \"Pricing settings\": the rates the calculator works from (hourly pay, holiday, NI, pension, materials, admin, travel per mile, target margin, minimum job price and minimum hours). Click \"Save settings\".\n\n### Quote history - page: /admin/quotes/history\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nOpened with \"History\". A table of all quotes. Search by client, prospect or description and filter by status. Click a quote to see its description, internal notes, shift pattern or calculator inputs, and price breakdown (all read only). A manually priced quote has no breakdown.\n\n### Quote wording - page: /admin/quotes/wording\n\nWho can use it: admins only (others see \"Only an admin can change the wording of quotes.\").\n\n- Each section of the quote document is listed. Change the \"Section title\" and \"Wording\", tick or untick \"Include\", set \"Appears on\" (\"Contract quotes only\", \"One-off quotes only\" or \"Both\") and \"Only for these services\".\n- Use the up and down arrows to move a section earlier or later.\n- Sections marked \"Built from the quote\" take their content from the quote itself (price, schedule, room list). You can retitle, move or switch them off, but there is no wording to edit.\n- Writing tips on the page: leave a blank line between paragraphs; start a line with \"## \" for a subheading or \"- \" for a bullet. Placeholders include {company}, {client}, {site} and {initial_period}.\n- Click \"Save section\" (or \"Discard\"). Changes apply to quotes generated from now on.\n\n---\n\n## Invoices (Clients → Invoices) - page: /admin/invoices\n\nWho can use it: one specific admin account only. Other admins and supervisors don't see it.\n\nThe page is titled \"Invoice breakdown\". It builds a month of visits for a client's QuickBooks invoice: each property with its dates, and room refreshes on their own lines. The app does not send invoices; you put them into QuickBooks.\n\nHow to build an invoice\n1. Choose the \"Client\" and \"Month\".\n2. Check \"Hourly rate (£)\". To change it, type a rate and click \"Save\".\n3. The page says which visits the invoice covers. Room refreshes are added on the rota by opening the visit.\n4. Read any \"Check before invoicing\" warnings.\n5. Use \"Copy the whole breakdown\", or the copy button on each line, and paste into QuickBooks. The page says what to use as quantity and rate. Some clients are charged per shift instead of per hour; the page says so.\n\nHow to download for QuickBooks import\n1. Under \"Put it into QuickBooks\", fill in \"Invoice number\" (the next one in QuickBooks), \"Invoice date\" and \"Product/service in QuickBooks\".\n2. Click \"Download for QuickBooks\".\n\n---\n\n## Cleaners (People → Cleaners) - page: /admin/cleaners\n\nWho can use it: admins only.\n\nThe page lists everyone with app access, with counts of cleaners, supervisors and inventory-only accounts. Each person shows warnings such as missing personal details or \"No bank details on file\". \"subcontractor\" marks people who invoice for their hours and accrue no holiday.\n\nHow to add a staff account directly\n1. Click \"+ Add staff\".\n2. Fill in \"Full name\", \"Email\" and \"Role\": \"Cleaner\", \"Office Staff / Supervisor\" or \"Inventory only\".\n3. Enter a \"Password\" (at least 8 characters) or click \"Generate\".\n4. Click \"Add staff\". You must share the password with them yourself, so note it down first.\n- Supervisors can manage the rota, clients and requests like an admin, but can't manage staff accounts or see payroll. Inventory only accounts can count and reorder stock and see nothing else.\n- For a new starter who should fill in their own details, ID and contract, use Onboarding instead.\n\nOther actions on the list\n- \"Adjust\" changes someone's holiday balance up or down (\"Manual adjustment (hours, +/-)\", then \"Save\").\n- \"Deactivate\" / \"Reactivate\" (see below).\n- \"Show former staff (N)\" shows removed and deactivated staff. Their shifts, hours and records are all still kept.\n\n### Cleaner page - /admin/cleaners/[id]\n\nWho can use it: admins only.\n\nAccount\n- \"Edit account\" changes \"Full name\", \"Login email\" (this changes what they sign in with, so tell them), \"Role\", and sets a new password (\"New password (leave blank to keep theirs)\", or \"Generate\"). Click \"Save account\".\n- Making someone a supervisor or inventory only asks you to confirm.\n- \"Can count and reorder stock\" adds the Stock screen to their app without changing their role.\n- For cleaners, \"Offer them shifts that need covering\". Untick it for someone on the books who does not cover cleans. They can still put their own shifts out for cover.\n\nThe \"...\" menu\n- \"Export data\": downloads everything held about the person, for a data request.\n- \"Deactivate\" / \"Reactivate\".\n- \"Remove account\": deactivates them and frees their email for reuse, keeping all their history. This can't be easily undone. If they still have keys signed out, you are warned (\"Keys not returned\") and asked to record them back in on the Key register first.\n- \"Delete account\": deletes the account completely. Only for an account never really used (added by mistake or a duplicate). If they have any shifts or history it is refused; use Remove instead.\n\nDeactivating\n- Deactivating signs the person out of the app on every device. They can't log in until reactivated. Their history is kept.\n\nDetails and records on the page\n- \"Personal details\": \"Edit\" or \"Add details\" for phone, address, date of birth, NI number and emergency contact. Staff can also keep these up to date from My Profile.\n- \"Bank details\": \"Add bank details\" or \"Replace\". Staff can add or change these from My Profile, and every change is announced to the office.\n- \"Onboarding record\": what they gave when they onboarded, kept as signed. \"View ID Document\" opens the ID they uploaded.\n- \"Absences\": missed shifts recorded against them.\n- \"Reliability score\": based on punctuality, completion rate, photo compliance and client rating, once there is enough history.\n- \"Certifications\": \"+ Certification\" adds a name, optional expiry date and notes (\"Add certification\"). Expiring ones appear on the Dashboard.\n- \"Holiday\": \"Mark time off\" (goes in already approved, and shifts on those days are put out for cover), \"Adjust\", and \"Mark as subcontractor\" / \"Mark as employee\". A subcontractor accrues no holiday and has holiday requests turned off; they can still say when they are unavailable.\n- \"1:1 Reviews\": \"+ Reminder\", with \"Repeats yearly\". Due ones appear on the Dashboard.\n- \"Upcoming\", \"Job History\" and \"Clock-in summary\" (\"Show\" / \"Hide\").\n\n---\n\n## Onboarding (People → Onboarding) - page: /admin/onboarding\n\nWho can use it: admins only.\n\nInvite links for new starters to set up their own account, and complete their details, ID and contract.\n\nHow to invite a new starter\n1. Click \"+ New invite\".\n2. Fill in \"Name\" and \"Email\" (required).\n3. Under \"Contract terms\", fill in \"Job title\", \"Hourly pay (£)\" (required), \"Paid\", \"Start date (optional)\" and \"Reports to\". These are written into the contract they sign. They can read them but not change them.\n4. Optional: \"Their details (optional)\" (home address, phone, date of birth). These are already on the form when they open the link, and they can correct them.\n5. Click \"Send invite\".\n6. The app emails the invite and shows the link. Click \"Copy\" to send it yourself as well.\n\nManaging invites\n- Each invite shows its status (pending, submitted or expired) and when a pending one expires.\n- \"Copy link\" copies a pending invite's link.\n- \"View details\" shows what they submitted, including the ID document (\"View document\") and the signed contract (\"Open PDF\").\n- \"Delete\" deletes the invite and the link stops working straight away. If it was already used, their submitted details are deleted too.\n- Once submitted, they appear in Cleaners.\n\n---\n\n## Payroll (People → Payroll) - page: /admin/payroll\n\nWho can use it: admins only.\n\nPayroll is where you check a pay period, lock it, and get a figure for QuickBooks that will not move. The dashboard's Staff hours panel is live and keeps changing; this page is the record.\n\nHow to close a pay period\n1. The top card names the \"Next period to close\" (or \"First period to close\"). It can be closed once the period has finished.\n2. Work through anything listed as still needing a decision. These include missed clock-in claims, short shifts to confirm or correct, jobs not finished, shifts nobody clocked into, and people who did not clock in on a shift a colleague worked. Each has a link (\"Open Requests\" or \"Open Rota\").\n3. When nothing is outstanding, you see \"Nothing outstanding - the figures below will not change once closed.\"\n4. Check \"What will be sent\". \"Show the N lines\" lists every job per person. To change what one person is paid for one job, use Requests, under Amend Hours.\n5. Optional: \"Note for the record (optional)\".\n6. Click \"Close period\" and confirm.\n7. The period is locked, each cleaner is told what went out, and you can download the CSV.\n\nRules\n- \"Close period\" stays disabled until the period has ended and nothing is outstanding.\n- Periods close in order.\n- If hours change on a period already closed, they appear under \"Waiting for the next run\" and go out as an adjustment on the next close. The old period is not rewritten.\n- For the very first close, \"Start the record from\" sets where the record begins.\n\nClosed periods\n- Each closed period is kept as a record of exactly what went out. \"Download CSV\" downloads it for QuickBooks.\n\nPay period schedule\n- At the bottom, set \"Frequency\" (\"Weekly\" or \"Monthly (calendar month)\") and \"Week starts on\", then click \"Save schedule\". Changing it only affects periods not yet closed.\n\n---\n\n## Training (People → Training) - page: /admin/training\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nThe page is titled \"Training videos\". These are the how-to videos cleaners see under Help. A video slot is hidden from cleaners until a file is uploaded.\n\nHow to add a video\n1. Click \"+ Video\".\n2. Fill in \"Title\", \"What it covers\" and \"Section\". Click \"Add slot\".\n3. On the new slot, click \"Upload file\" and choose a video file. You see that it is now live for cleaners.\n\nManaging videos\n- \"Replace file\" uploads a new file for the same slot.\n- \"Preview\" lets you watch it.\n- \"Edit\" changes the title, wording or section.\n- \"Take down\" hides it from cleaners but keeps the slot and its wording.\n- \"Delete\" removes the slot, the file and the record of who watched it, for good.\n- The arrows move a video earlier or later in the running order.\n- Each video shows how many cleaners watched it to the end, and how many started it.\n\n---\n\n## Templates (Records → Templates) - page: /admin/templates\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nThe page is titled \"Job templates\". A template is a reusable checklist you can apply to any job.\n\nHow to make a template\n1. Click \"+ New template\".\n2. Fill in \"Name\" and the \"Checklist items\". \"+ Add item\" adds a line; \"Remove\" deletes one.\n3. Click \"Save template\".\n\nUsing and editing\n- Apply a template when booking a job (\"Checklist template (optional)\") or from the job panel (\"Apply a template...\" then \"Apply\").\n- On the Templates page, \"Edit\" shows the tasks. Add a task and click \"Add\", or \"Remove\" one.\n- \"Delete\" deletes the template. Jobs it was already applied to keep their tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Documents (Records → Documents) - page: /admin/documents\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nPolicies, contracts and other files shared with staff.\n\nHow to share a document with staff\n1. Under \"Upload\", choose a \"Category\" (Policy, Contract or Other).\n2. Under \"Share with\", choose \"Everyone\" or \"Certain cleaners\" (then tick the cleaners).\n3. Choose one or more files under \"Files\". They upload straight away under that category.\n4. Each document shows who it is shared with.\n\nDownload or delete with the icons. Deleting means staff can no longer see or download it.\n\nDocuments for a single client are uploaded on that client's page instead (Documents tab).\n\n---\n\n## Inventory (Records → Inventory) - page: /admin/inventory\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office, and staff with the stock permission or an Inventory only account.\n\nHow to add a product\n1. Click \"+ Product\".\n2. Fill in \"Product name\", \"Starting stock\", \"Reorder threshold\", and optionally \"Location\", \"Supplier\" and \"Unit price\".\n3. Click \"Add product\".\n\nHow to do a stock count\n1. Under \"Stock levels\", use the minus and plus buttons, or type the count. Search by name, location or supplier.\n2. Counting changes nothing until you click \"Save stock\". \"Discard\" puts the counts back.\n3. Leaving with unsaved changes asks whether to discard them.\n\nShopping list\n- Items below their reorder level appear under \"Shopping list\".\n- Download it as \"Word\", \"Excel\" or \"PDF\". These are disabled until stock changes are saved.\n\nRemoving a product: click the remove button on it and confirm.\n\n---\n\n## Key register (Records → Key register) - page: /admin/keys\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nEvery key, fob and access code issued: who holds it now and the signed handover trail. Never type the actual alarm code or key-safe number here. The register records who was given it and when it came back, not the code itself.\n\nHow to add a key\n1. Click \"Add key\".\n2. Choose the \"Site\", the \"Type\" (Key, Fob, Alarm code, Other), a \"Label\" and optional \"Notes\".\n3. Click \"Add key\". It starts off in the office, not issued to anyone.\n\nHow to issue a key\n1. Find the key under its site and click \"Issue\".\n2. Choose \"Issue to\", and optionally \"Due back\" and a \"Note\".\n3. Click \"Issue key\". The person is asked to sign for it in the app.\n- \"Unsigned\" shows until they sign. \"Overdue\" shows when it is past its due-back date.\n\nHow to record a key coming back\n1. Click the return icon (\"Record return\") on the key, either under \"Out now\" or under the site.\n2. Confirm.\n\nRetiring and deleting\n- The archive icon retires a key that is in the office. It stays on the record with its history but can't be issued again.\n- A key that is out must be recorded back in first.\n- A retired key shows \"Delete\", which removes it and its handover history for good.\n- The history icon shows everyone who has held a key.\n- Removing a staff account warns you if they still hold keys.\n\n---\n\n## Accidents and incidents (Records → Accidents and incidents) - page: /admin/incidents\n\nWho can use it: admins only (injury details are health data).\n\nThis is the accident book. Staff report from their phones, or you can add a report yourself. Reports are kept for at least three years and can't be deleted, and the original account can't be changed.\n\nThe top shows counts: still open, needing an HSE decision or report, and accidents, incidents and near misses in the last 12 months.\n\nHow to add a report yourself\n1. Click \"Add a report\".\n2. Under \"What happened?\", choose \"Someone got hurt\" (accident), \"Something went wrong\" (incident) or \"It nearly happened\" (near miss).\n3. Fill in the form: who told you, when it happened (for an old entry, use the real date and time), where, what happened, and, for an accident, who was hurt, the injury and treatment. Photos are optional.\n4. Click \"Add the report\".\n\nHow to work through a report\n1. Filter with \"Still open\", \"Closed\" or \"All\", and by type.\n2. Click a report to open it. \"What's left to do\" lists what is still needed.\n3. Fill in the sections: \"The person who was hurt\" (address, job, whether they work for you, body part, time off work); \"Does HSE need to know?\" (answer the questions and the app tells you whether it does); \"Putting it right\" (seriousness, risk assessment review, cause, what you've done); and \"Who you've told\" (dates you told your insurer and the client).\n4. If HSE needs to know, use \"Open HSE's report form\" and \"Copy the details to paste in\". Then record the date you reported it and HSE's reference number.\n5. Click \"Save\". When the list is done, click \"Save and close\". The person who reported it is told it is closed, and sees what you've done so it doesn't happen again.\n6. \"Reopen\" opens a closed report again.\n- Once saved, the injured person's name, address and job can't be changed.\n- Badges show \"Check if HSE needs to know\", \"Report to HSE by ...\", \"HSE report overdue\" or \"Reported to HSE\".\n\nSite warnings\n- In a report, \"Warn the next cleaner\" lets you choose a site and write a warning, then \"Add the warning\". Everyone sent to a job at that site sees it on the job page.\n- Describe the danger, not the person; staff can read it.\n- \"Site warnings staff can see\" lists current warnings. Click \"Fixed\" once the danger has gone; staff stop seeing it.\n\n\"Download\" saves the reports shown as a spreadsheet.\n\n---\n\n## Insights (Records → Insights) - page: /admin/insights\n\nWho can use it: admins only (it is built from everyone's hours).\n\nThe last 12 weeks at a glance. Figures are the last 4 weeks unless a chart says otherwise, and arrows compare with the 4 weeks before.\n- Figures: \"Hours worked\", \"Visits completed\", \"Visits missed\", \"Arrived on time\".\n- Charts: \"Hours worked\" per week, \"Visits\" per week (completed and missed), \"Clients by hours\", and \"Arriving on time\" per person (clocked in within 5 minutes of the start, for staff with enough clock-ins).\n\n---\n\n## Reports (Records → Reports) - page: /admin/reports\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nAI-written job reports for jobs that are in progress or completed. The page subtitle reads \"AI-generated job reports — visible to admins only\"; cleaners do not see them, and a client only sees one if you tick \"Add to client portal\". Filter with \"Needs a report\", \"Report written\" or \"All\", and search by address.\n\nHow to write a report\n1. Click \"Generate report\" on a job.\n2. Choose a \"Template\".\n3. Type a few notes, or click \"Speak notes\" to dictate (works in Chrome).\n4. Click \"Generate report\". It is written from your notes and the job's photos.\n\nAfter it is written\n- \"View report\" shows it.\n- Tick \"Add to client portal\" to let the client see it.\n- \"Regenerate\" writes it again from new notes; the current report is replaced.\n- \"Download PDF\" saves it with its photos.\n\n### Monthly reports - page: /admin/reports/monthly\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nOpened with \"Monthly reports\". Choose a \"Client\" and \"Month\" to see a month of visits at each property, with every shared report and its photos. Clients with detailed reports switched on can also read and download these in their portal under Reports. For other clients you can still download and send them.\n\n---\n\n## Data reports (Records → Data reports) - page: /admin/data-reports\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nPull data and download it as a spreadsheet.\n1. Choose a report: \"Clients\", \"Staff\", \"Hours Worked\", \"Jobs History\", \"Quotes\", \"Properties\" or \"Time Off\".\n2. For Hours Worked and Jobs History, choose a period (\"All time\", \"This week\", \"Last week\", \"This month\", \"Last month\").\n3. Click \"Download CSV\".\n\n---\n\n## Help (Help) - page: /admin/help\n\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n\nShort notes on common tasks, a link to the Privacy Notice, and \"Data retention\".\n\nData retention\n- Runs automatically every night. It redacts personal details (and deletes any ID document on file) for deactivated staff, and for clients marked \"relationship ended\", once 6 years have passed.\n- \"Run retention sweep now\" runs it straight away and reports how many records were redacted.\n\nSome notes on the Help page are older than the app. Where they differ, this guide follows the app: for example, the new client form does not add a property (add it on the client's page), and the cleaner's button is \"Can't make this shift\".\n\n---\n\n## What cleaners see and do (for the office)\n\nCleaners use their own app. Only the parts that affect the office are listed here.\n\n- Check in: on a job, they tap \"Check in\". Their location is checked against the property pin. Check-in opens on the day of the shift; before that the button says \"Not open yet\". If the shift time has passed they can still check in.\n- Wrong pin: if they are too far away, they can tap \"I'm at the property — check in here\". The office is asked to move the pin (Requests → Property pins).\n- One shift at a time: they must check out of one shift before checking in to another.\n- Check out: \"Check out\". If they took no photos, or areas have no photo, they are warned and can \"Check out anyway\".\n- More time: \"More time\" asks the office for a time extension (Requests → Time extensions).\n- Can't make it: \"Can't make this shift\" puts the shift out for cover. It stays theirs until the office approves someone else (Shift cover).\n- Picking up cover: they see \"Shifts needing cover\" and tap \"Ask for this shift\". The office approves who gets it.\n- Forgot to clock in: \"I worked this — I forgot to clock in\" sends a claim (Requests → Missed clock-ins).\n- Time off: they request holiday or unavailability from their rota (Requests → Time off).\n- Job notes and access: they see the job's \"Notes\", the property's notes, and the access details once assigned. They also see any site warnings.\n- Keys: they are asked to sign for keys issued to them.\n- Announcements pop up until they tap \"Got it\".\n- Accident reports: they can report from their phone, and if there is no signal the report is kept on the phone and sends itself later.\n\n---\n\n## Common questions\n\n**How do I give a cleaner a shift?**\nOpen the Rota and click \"New job\", pick the client, address, date, time and duration, click the cleaner's name under \"Cleaners\", and click \"Add job\". For an existing job, open it and use \"Add a cleaner...\" then \"Add\". They get a notification.\n\n**Why can't I delete this job?**\nCompleted and missed visits stay on the record and can't be deleted. On a recurring job you can still use \"Delete future visits\" to remove the visits after it.\n\n**Why can't I change the time of this job?**\nDate and time can only be changed while a job is still scheduled. Once it has started or finished, add a new job instead.\n\n**Why can't I remove a cleaner from this job?**\nThe visit is completed or missed, so the staff on it can't be changed. To change what someone is paid for it, click \"Hours\" next to their name.\n\n**I removed a cleaner from a recurring job. Will it take them off every visit?**\nOnly if you choose so. Remove asks \"Just this visit\", \"This visit and N later in this series\" or \"This visit and all N later at this site\". Earlier and finished visits are never changed.\n\n**A cleaner can't make their shift. What do I do?**\nThey tap \"Can't make this shift\", or you click \"Request cover\" on Shift cover. Then approve someone who asked, or click \"Assign\" and pick someone. The shift stays with the original cleaner until you do.\n\n**Someone rang in sick. How do I record it?**\nGo to Requests → Time off and click \"+ Mark time off\". Choose \"Unavailable\" (or \"Holiday\"), the dates, and click \"Mark as unavailable\". If they have shifts in that time, you can put them out for cover.\n\n**What happens when I deactivate a cleaner?**\nThey are signed out on every device and can't log in until reactivated. Their history is kept. Only admins can do this, from Cleaners.\n\n**What is the difference between Deactivate, Remove account and Delete account?**\nDeactivate blocks sign-in and can be undone. Remove account also frees their email for a new starter and keeps their history; it is warned if they still hold keys. Delete account removes everything and only works for an account with no shifts or history.\n\n**Why can't I close payroll?**\n\"Close period\" stays disabled until the period has ended and nothing is outstanding. Clear the items listed (missed clock-ins, short shifts, unfinished jobs and so on) in Requests or the Rota.\n\n**A cleaner forgot to clock in but did the work. How do they get paid?**\nIn Requests → Missed clock-ins, approve their claim, or click \"They worked it\" on the shift. Otherwise the shift is unpaid.\n\n**I changed someone's hours after payroll closed. What happens?**\nIt appears under \"Waiting for the next run\" on Payroll and goes out as an adjustment on the next close. The closed period is not changed.\n\n**Where do I put the alarm code or key safe code for a site?**\nOn the client's page, click \"Access\" on the property and save it. The cleaner sees it on their job once assigned. Don't put codes in the Key register.\n\n**A cleaner can't check in because they're \"too far away\". What can I do?**\nThey can tap \"I'm at the property — check in here\". You then get a Property pins request: click \"Move pin here\" if it's right. You can also move the pin or widen the \"Check-in radius (metres)\" from \"Location\" on the client's page.\n\n**Why can't a cleaner check in yet?**\nCheck-in opens on the day of the shift. Before that, the button says \"Not open yet\".\n\n**How do I send a message to every cleaner?**\nUse Announcements. Fill in a headline and message and click \"Send to all staff (N)\". Tick \"Also send a phone notification\" to ring their phones too.\n\n**Why can't I see Payroll, Cleaners or Insights?**\nThey are admins only. Supervisors don't see them in the menu. Invoices is limited to one admin account.\n\n**How do I send a quote to a client?**\nDownload it with \"PDF\" (or \"Word\" to edit first) and send it yourself. Then set its status to \"Sent\".\n\n**Can I delete an accident report?**\nNo. Reports are kept for at least three years and can't be deleted. You can add to them and close them.\n\n**How do I make a repeating weekly clean?**\nIn the new job form, tick \"Repeat this job\", choose \"Weekly\", tick the days, and set when it ends. Up to 104 visits can be booked at once.\n\n## Ask WorkFleet (the chat in the bottom-right corner)\nWho can use it: everyone in the office.\n- Click \"Ask\" in the bottom-right corner of any office page to ask how to do something.\n- You can also ask it to book a visit, move a visit, put a cleaner on or take one off a visit, or change a visit's notes. Each change appears as a card with any warnings (double-bookings, time off). Nothing happens until you click \"Confirm\" on the card; \"No thanks\" leaves it.\n- It cannot delete visits, change a whole repeating job, set split hours or change finished visits - do those on the Rota page.\n- The circular arrow at the top starts a new conversation.\n";
